<title>BRAZIL: Brazil gov't to sell minority shrs in firms Monday.</title>
<headline>Brazil gov't to sell minority shrs in firms Monday.</headline>
<dateline>RIO DE JANEIRO 1996-12-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>On behalf of the federal government,  Brazil's National Development Bank (BNDES) said it will auction Monday a portfolio of minority shares in several firms including Telebras, Telemig and Petrobras.</p>
<p>BNDES said the federal government will also sell shares in pulp and paper firm Aracruz, Minas Gerais state power firm Cemig and Rio Grande do Sul state's telecoms Companhia Riograndense de Telecomunicacoes (CRT), among others.</p>
<p>The shares, which are worth around 30 million reais, will be sold at an auction at 1200 local/1400 GMT on the Rio de Janeiro Stock Exchange.</p>
<p>((--Fatima Cristina, Rio de Janeiro Newsroom 5521 5074151))</p>
